   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ בְּהֵמָה גַּסָּה נִקְנֵית בִּמְסִירָה, וְהַדַּקָּה בְּהַגְבָּהָה, דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי מֵאִיר וְרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר. וַחֲכָמִים אוֹמְרִים: בְּהֵמָה דַּקָּה נִקְנֵית בִּמְשִׁיכָה.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «A large domesticated animal is acquired by passing,» when its current owner transfers it to a buyer by giving him the reins or the bit. «And a small» domesticated animal is acquired «by lifting.» This is «the statement of Rabbi Meir and Rabbi Eliezer. And the Rabbis say: A small domesticated animal can be acquired by pulling» also, and there is no need to lift it."
  }
